 ## Overview
-Coverage-Aware Pruning is a density control strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting that prevents the premature removal of primitives required by specific training presets or camera views. It differs from standard opacity pruning by evaluating the maximum effective opacity across all training configurations, ensuring that Gaussians contributing to any single preset survive even if they are transparent in others [S2, unofficial]. It replaces the opacity reset mechanism used in standard 3DGS [S1].
+Coverage-Aware Pruning prevents the premature removal of Gaussians that are transparent in most views but critical for specific training presets or camera configurations [S1][S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard opacity pruning by evaluating the maximum effective opacity across all training configurations, ensuring that Gaussians contributing to any single preset survive even if they are transparent in others [S2, unofficial]. It replaces the opacity reset mechanism used in standard 3DGS [S1].
 
